{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type ApplyJoinOptionalityToMergedSchema<TExistingSchema, TNewSchema, TJoinType, TFromSourceNames> = { [K in keyof TExistingSchema]: K extends TFromSourceNames ? TJoinType extends \"right\" | \"full\" ? TExistingSchema[K] | undefined : TExistingSchema[K] : TExistingSchema[K] } & { [K in keyof TNewSchema]: TJoinType extends \"left\" | \"full\" ? TNewSchema[K] | undefined : TNewSchema[K] };","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts#L1037","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts:1037"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ApplyJoinOptionalityToMergedSchema - Applies optionality rules when merging schemas"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This type implements the SQL join optionality semantics:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Existing Tables"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RIGHT JOIN"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FULL JOIN"},{"type":"text","value":": Main table (from fromSourceName) becomes optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other join types: Existing tables keep their current optionality"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Previously joined tables: Keep their already-applied optionality"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For New Tables"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LEFT JOIN"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FULL JOIN"},{"type":"text","value":": New table becomes optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"INNER JOIN"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RIGHT JOIN"},{"type":"text","value":": New table remains required"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"FROM users LEFT JOIN orders  -- orders becomes optional\nFROM users RIGHT JOIN orders -- users becomes optional\nFROM users FULL JOIN orders  -- both become optional\nFROM users INNER JOIN orders -- both remain required","lang":"sql"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The intersection (&) ensures both existing and new schemas are merged\ninto a single type while preserving all table references."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"texistingschema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TExistingSchema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TExistingSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"ContextSchema.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ContextSchema"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tnewschema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TNewSchema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TNewSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"ContextSchema.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ContextSchema"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tjointype","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TJoinType"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TJoinType"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"inner\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"left\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"right\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"full\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"outer\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"cross\""}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfromsourcenames","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFromSourceNames"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFromSourceNames"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"texistingschema","text":"TExistingSchema","level":3},{"id":"tnewschema","text":"TNewSchema","level":3},{"id":"tjointype","text":"TJoinType","level":3},{"id":"tfromsourcenames","text":"TFromSourceNames","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype ApplyJoinOptionalityToMergedSchema<TExistingSchema, TNewSchema, TJoinType, TFromSourceNames> = { [K in keyof TExistingSchema]: K extends TFromSourceNames ? TJoinType extends \"right\" | \"full\" ? TExistingSchema[K] | undefined : TExistingSchema[K] : TExistingSchema[K] } & { [K in keyof TNewSchema]: TJoinType extends \"left\" | \"full\" ? TNewSchema[K] | undefined : TNewSchema[K] };\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts:1037](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts#L1037)\n\nApplyJoinOptionalityToMergedSchema - Applies optionality rules when merging schemas\n\nThis type implements the SQL join optionality semantics:\n\n**For Existing Tables**:\n- `RIGHT JOIN` or `FULL JOIN`: Main table (from fromSourceName) becomes optional\n- Other join types: Existing tables keep their current optionality\n- Previously joined tables: Keep their already-applied optionality\n\n**For New Tables**:\n- `LEFT JOIN` or `FULL JOIN`: New table becomes optional\n- `INNER JOIN` or `RIGHT JOIN`: New table remains required\n\n**Examples**:\n```sql\nFROM users LEFT JOIN orders  -- orders becomes optional\nFROM users RIGHT JOIN orders -- users becomes optional\nFROM users FULL JOIN orders  -- both become optional\nFROM users INNER JOIN orders -- both remain required\n```\n\nThe intersection (&) ensures both existing and new schemas are merged\ninto a single type while preserving all table references.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TExistingSchema\n\n`TExistingSchema` *extends* [`ContextSchema`](ContextSchema.md)\n\n### TNewSchema\n\n`TNewSchema` *extends* [`ContextSchema`](ContextSchema.md)\n\n### TJoinType\n\n`TJoinType` *extends* `\"inner\"` \\| `\"left\"` \\| `\"right\"` \\| `\"full\"` \\| `\"outer\"` \\| `\"cross\"`\n\n### TFromSourceNames\n\n`TFromSourceNames` *extends* `string`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ApplyJoinOptionalityToMergedSchema\ntitle: ApplyJoinOptionalityToMergedSchema\n---\n\n```ts\ntype ApplyJoinOptionalityToMergedSchema<TExistingSchema, TNewSchema, TJoinType, TFromSourceNames> = { [K in keyof TExistingSchema]: K extends TFromSourceNames ? TJoinType extends \"right\" | \"full\" ? TExistingSchema[K] | undefined : TExistingSchema[K] : TExistingSchema[K] } & { [K in keyof TNewSchema]: TJoinType extends \"left\" | \"full\" ? TNewSchema[K] | undefined : TNewSchema[K] };\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts:1037](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts#L1037)\n\nApplyJoinOptionalityToMergedSchema - Applies optionality rules when merging schemas\n\nThis type implements the SQL join optionality semantics:\n\n**For Existing Tables**:\n- `RIGHT JOIN` or `FULL JOIN`: Main table (from fromSourceName) becomes optional\n- Other join types: Existing tables keep their current optionality\n- Previously joined tables: Keep their already-applied optionality\n\n**For New Tables**:\n- `LEFT JOIN` or `FULL JOIN`: New table becomes optional\n- `INNER JOIN` or `RIGHT JOIN`: New table remains required\n\n**Examples**:\n```sql\nFROM users LEFT JOIN orders  -- orders becomes optional\nFROM users RIGHT JOIN orders -- users becomes optional\nFROM users FULL JOIN orders  -- both become optional\nFROM users INNER JOIN orders -- both remain required\n```\n\nThe intersection (&) ensures both existing and new schemas are merged\ninto a single type while preserving all table references.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TExistingSchema\n\n`TExistingSchema` *extends* [`ContextSchema`](ContextSchema.md)\n\n### TNewSchema\n\n`TNewSchema` *extends* [`ContextSchema`](ContextSchema.md)\n\n### TJoinType\n\n`TJoinType` *extends* `\"inner\"` \\| `\"left\"` \\| `\"right\"` \\| `\"full\"` \\| `\"outer\"` \\| `\"cross\"`\n\n### TFromSourceNames\n\n`TFromSourceNames` *extends* `string`\n"}
